      "title": "Letterboxd review of No Time to Die",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"No Time to Die\"] Film #25 of March Around the World 2017Country: GhanaIf this shows its low budget and amateur performers, it's also a fun romantic comedy. The lead characters are both likeable people and their romance is one that can be believed. There's no outlandish contrivance here. Simply two people who meet and take an interest in one another. If David Dontoh is more comfortable in front of the camera than Agatha Ofori, who comes off a bit like someone on stage for the first time at the local community theatre, I've seen big name stars in well funded US productions that I liked a lot less than these two.",
